<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diplomystus dentatus detail-tier Turing wavelength (184.3 µm, 51.5 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2. Same Schnakenberg onset wavelength, 184.3 µm at 51.5 Ma. Radial peak remains 186.0 µm (dispersion r=1.000, RMSE=0.00033; diffusivity sweep r=0.997). Remediation: a Dy/Dx=1.8 dorsoventral trial selected 212 µm (15% off the onset law) and was rejected, so the isotropic field is kept. A 1e-5 cubic equal-diffusion perturbation decays (std ratio 0.118), in addition to the linearised ratio 0.031. Five minor-axis transects on the Descouens fish give a central spacing of 6.33 mm with a placement std of 11.7 mm, so the fossil spacing is millimetre-scale and is not the 0.1843 mm wave. The assessor is still a single agent. Overall 86.4/100 (faithfulness 85.7, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/diplomystus_dentatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 1060255 B, 1736×1176 px, artifact_sha256 f34d3f2bca1546c3fc700886b5df0c81361bd0043fc5509294d28170e4b06697 (sha256 f34d3f2bca1546c3fc700886b5df0c81361bd0043fc5509294d28170e4b06697), spec_fingerprint dca96e708aacc37802c4b54ab60381864ab6fced4c5a2aa1dbd4e8eeec3dd5e9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dca96e708aacc37802c4b54ab60381864ab6fced4c5a2aa1dbd4e8eeec3dd5e9; artifact_sha256: f34d3f2bca1546c3fc700886b5df0c81361bd0043fc5509294d28170e4b06697. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-diplomystus-dentatus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) onset wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), lambda_c = 2 pi / k_c. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Grande (1982) redescribes Diplomystus dentatus from the Fossil Butte Member: dorsal scutes usually 22-36, maximum length about 65 cm, ellimmichthyid rather than a clupeid. | Kondo & Asai (1995) and Nakamasu et al. (2009) show teleost skin can select a Turing pigment wavelength. | Smith, Carroll & Singer (2008) reconstruct the Eocene Green River lake system. Descouens' CC BY-SA 4.0 photograph is a Fossil Lake specimen with caption size 48 cm.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.128, b=0.764, D_v/D_u=9.17, with D_u solved so the onset wavelength is 184.3 µm. Neumann explicit Euler on a flank window. These constants belong to slot 3170, not to the 7.56 mm sibling. | Discrete-Laplacian growth rates versus the analytic eigenvalue (Pearson r = 1.000, RMSE = 0.00033) and a diffusivity sweep of expressed wavelength (Pearson r = 0.997). | Equal-diffusion ablation (linearised std ratio 0.031) and a 20 µm predecessor mode with negative growth rate. | Segmentation of the Descouens photograph: aspect ratio, circularity, and a high-pass major-axis spacing used as an organ-scale contrast to 0.1843 mm.; transfer_boundary: Pigment kinetics are transferred from the teleost Turing literature onto a Diplomystus flank. The 184.3 µm value is the catalogued detail tier, not a melanophore count on the slab. | 51.5 Ma is the Ypresian chronoseries datum. The series contains one Diplomystus age (1/1); the predecessor and successor compared here are scales, not other chronospecies.; does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 184 µm ocelli, or that a, b, and D were measured in Diplomystus tissue. | That dorsal scute counts (22-36) are the same pattern as the detail-tier wave. | A new radiometric date for Fossil Lake.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Still a single builder-assessor. A second provider was not available; no second score was invented.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.64e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

